title: Select several at once
intro: Ctrl and Shift pick several entities in the Hierarchy, and delete, duplicate, cut, copy and paste work on all of them.
project: Platformer | Multi Select

chapter: Picking several | Ctrl and Shift in the Hierarchy
say: Until now the Hierarchy picked one entity at a time. Now it picks as many as you like.
select: Slime
select: Ctrl+Checkpoint
select: Ctrl+Sign
expectselected: Slime, Checkpoint, Sign
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Ctrl-click | Control click adds a row to the selection. The slime, the checkpoint and the sign are all picked.
explain: scene | All outlined | The Scene view outlines every one of them. The last one picked gets the move handle.
explain: panel:Inspector | All three | The Inspector shows what all three have in common, to edit together.
select: Ctrl+Checkpoint
expectselected: Slime, Sign
say: Control click on a picked row takes it out again.
select: Lever
select: Shift+Sign
expectselected: Lever, Checkpoint, Sign
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Shift-click | Shift click picks every row from the last one clicked, here the lever down to the sign.

chapter: Acting on all of them | One undo step each
select: Slime
select: Ctrl+Coins
say: Control D duplicates everything picked. Each copy goes right after its original, and the copies end up selected.
key: Ctrl+D
expectcount: Slime = 2
expectcount: Coin = 12
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Copies | A second slime, and a second row of coins.
say: However many there were, it's one step to undo.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectcount: Slime = 1
expectcount: Coin = 8
select: Slime
select: Ctrl+Lever
say: Delete removes them all at once.
key: Delete
expectcount: Slime = 0
expectcount: Lever = 0
key: Ctrl+Z
expectcount: Lever = 1
say: And undo brings them all back, each where it was.

chapter: Cut and paste | Moving several together
select: Slime
select: Ctrl+Sign
say: Cut and paste move several together. Cut the slime and the sign, pick the music, and paste.
key: Ctrl+X
expectcount: Slime = 0
select: Music
key: Ctrl+V
expectselected: Slime, Sign
explain: panel:Hierarchy | Pasted | They land after the music, in their order, still selected and ready for the next thing.
say: Copy works the same way, and what's copied pastes into another scene too.
